<%- include('../partials/head', { pageTitle, metaDescription, canonicalPath }) %>
<%- include('../partials/header') %>
<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Size guide</h1>
      <p class="lede mt-1">Measure at home. These are the numbers we actually manufacture to.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 id="rings">Ring sizes (Indian)</h2>
        <p>
          Wrap a strip of paper or a piece of non-stretch string around the base of the finger, snug but not tight.
          Mark where it meets, measure the length in millimetres, and match it to the circumference column. If you
          are between two sizes, choose the larger one — a ring that is slightly loose is easier to size than one
          that will not go over the knuckle.
        </p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Indian size</th><th scope="col">Inner diameter</th><th scope="col">Circumference</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>12</td><td>16.5 mm</td><td>51.8 mm</td></tr>
            <tr><td>14</td><td>17.3 mm</td><td>54.4 mm</td></tr>
            <tr><td>16</td><td>18.1 mm</td><td>56.9 mm</td></tr>
            <tr><td>18</td><td>18.9 mm</td><td>59.5 mm</td></tr>
            <tr><td>20</td><td>19.8 mm</td><td>62.1 mm</td></tr>
            <tr><td>22</td><td>20.6 mm</td><td>64.6 mm</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="small">
          Measure at the end of the day when your fingers are at their usual size, and avoid measuring when cold.
          Wide bands (4 mm and above) feel tighter than thin ones — size up if you are between sizes on a wide band.
        </p>

        <h2 id="chains">Chain lengths</h2>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Length</th><th scope="col">Where it sits</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>45 cm</td><td>At the base of the neck. Reads as a collar chain.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>50 cm</td><td>Just below the collarbone. Our default and the most versatile.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>55 cm</td><td>Mid-chest, works over a tee or hoodie.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="small">All lengths are measured end to end, clasp included.</p>

        <h2 id="bracelets">Bracelets</h2>
        <p>
          Measure your wrist circumference snugly with a strip of paper, then add 1–1.5 cm for comfort. A flat-link
          bracelet should sit still on the wrist with a little room to move.
        </p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Wrist</th><th scope="col">Choose</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>14–16 cm</td><td>18 cm</td></tr>
            <tr><td>16–18 cm</td><td>20 cm</td></tr>
            <tr><td>18–20 cm</td><td>22 cm</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 id="cuffs">Cuffs and adjustable pieces</h2>
        <p>
          Our Plain Cuff is open and adjusts by roughly ±5 mm by hand at the ends. Repeated bending will eventually
          weaken any metal, so set it once and leave it.
        </p>

        <div class="callout callout--info">
          <strong>Still not sure?</strong> Message support with your measurement and the piece you are looking at.
          We would rather answer a question than process a return.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
<%- include('../partials/consent-banner') %>
</body>
</html>
